From a7427db72baa6e67afbae435ddf18e2443df663e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 15:31:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] zx279128s: drop the mii command to stay inside the v3 size
 gate (task-92)

The unified E4 v3 build came out at 410040 bytes, 2488 bytes over the
407552-byte budget (653312-byte hard cap minus 245760 bytes of headroom).
Per the 2026-11-28 budget ruling, reclaim the pre-approved P2 before
touching the rescue page: the console mii command is a debugging
convenience (cmd/mii.o measured 5696 text + 28 data in the v2.1 build) and
no boot or rescue path uses it; the board-local e2631net diagnostics and
the PHY startup logs cover the same ground.

The page I18N stays intact: I18N is preserved ahead of mii.

Signed-off-by: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
---
 configs/zx279128s_zte_zxhn-e2631_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configs/zx279128s_zte_zxhn-e2631_defconfig b/configs/zx279128s_zte_zxhn-e2631_defconfig
index 5fd993bb..38c98bc2 100644
--- a/configs/zx279128s_zte_zxhn-e2631_defconfig
+++ b/configs/zx279128s_zte_zxhn-e2631_defconfig
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ CONFIG_CMD_MEMTEST=y
 CONFIG_CMD_MTD=y
 # CONFIG_CMD_MTD_WRITE is not set
 CONFIG_CMD_DHCP=y
-CONFIG_CMD_MII=y
+# CONFIG_CMD_MII is not set
 CONFIG_CMD_PING=y
 # CONFIG_CMD_TFTPBOOT is not set
 CONFIG_OF_CONTROL=y
-- 
